"<main>\n  <section class=\"wrap hero\" id=\"check\">\n    <div>\n      <h1><span>See who can spend.</span><span>Cut unwanted access.</span></h1>\n      <p class=\"lede\">Apps and AI agents on Tempo get spending power through access keys. Keycut finds every key on an account and tells you what each one can do.</p>\n      <form class=\"search\" id=\"search\" novalidate>\n        <label class=\"sr\" for=\"addr\">Account address</label>\n        <input id=\"addr\" placeholder=\"Paste a Tempo account address\" autocomplete=\"off\" spellcheck=\"false\">\n        <button class=\"btn btn-cut\" type=\"submit\" id=\"find\">Find keys</button>\n      </form>\n      <p class=\"fine\" id=\"searchmsg\">Read-only. No wallet needed to look.</p>\n      <div class=\"alts\"><a href=\"/demo\">Try the live demo</a><a href=\"/testnet/0xE5CB1Dd82e60Df2A1cd6b58dF218aea7d535521A\">See a leftover key</a></div>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"ledger\" id=\"ledger\" aria-live=\"polite\">\n      <div class=\"scanbar\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></div>\n      <div class=\"ledger-head\"><span>Testnet account <span class=\"mono\">0xE5CB\u2026521A</span></span><span id=\"found\">Reading keys\u2026</span></div>\n      <p class=\"verdict\"><span id=\"verdict\">&nbsp;</span></p>\n      <div class=\"rows\" id=\"rows\"></div>\n      <p class=\"ledger-foot\">Seeded testnet example. Cut animation only, no transaction. <button class=\"replay\" id=\"replay\">Replay</button></p>\n    </div>\n  </section>\n\n  <div class=\"wrap\"><div class=\"cutline\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></div></div>\n\n  <section class=\"wrap numbers\">\n    <p class=\"big\" id=\"bignum\">{{STATS}}</p>\n    <p class=\"small\">{{DETAIL}} No tool we found lists these keys. Token-approval checkers don\u2019t cover access keys.</p>\n  </section>\n\n  <section class=\"wrap\">\n    <div class=\"story\">\n      <h2>The leftover key</h2>\n      <p>On Tempo, revoking an admin key doesn't revoke the keys it created. Retire an agent and the access it handed out can stay behind.</p>\n      <ol class=\"steps\" id=\"steps\">\n        <li><div><h3>An agent gets an admin key</h3><p>It can create and revoke other keys on your account.</p></div></li>\n        <li><div><h3>It creates a key for itself</h3><p>A child key with its own cap, payees and expiry.</p></div></li>\n        <li><div><h3>You retire the agent</h3><p>You revoke its admin key and move on.</p></div></li>\n        <li class=\"alarm\"><div><h3>The child key still spends</h3><p>Nothing on the chain links it back. Keycut finds it.</p></div></li>\n      </ol>\n      <div class=\"ctas\"><a class=\"btn btn-cut\" href=\"/demo\">Run the live demo</a><a class=\"btn btn-line\" href=\"/testnet/0xE5CB1Dd82e60Df2A1cd6b58dF218aea7d535521A\">See a leftover key</a></div>\n    </div>\n  </section>\n\n  <section class=\"wrap how\" id=\"how\">\n    <div>\n      <h2>How it works</h2>\n      <p>Keycut reads Tempo's key system directly. Looking is read-only. Cut access in the seeded demo or use the owner command on a real account.</p>\n    </div>\n    <ol>\n      <li>\n        <div class=\"frag\" id=\"frag1\"><span class=\"mono\" id=\"typed\"></span><span class=\"caret\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span></div>\n        <div><h3>Paste an address</h3><p>Any Tempo account, on testnet or mainnet. Keycut checks indexed history and the latest blocks, with coverage shown.</p></div>\n      </li>\n      <li>\n        <div class=\"frag\" id=\"frag2\"><div class=\"kv\"><span>Cap</span><span class=\"risk\">No cap</span><span>Pays</span><span class=\"risk\">Anyone</span><span>Ends</span><span>Never</span></div></div>\n        <div><h3>Read every key</h3><p>How much each key can spend, who it can pay and when it ends, with the risky ones flagged.</p></div>\n      </li>\n      <li>\n        <div class=\"frag\" id=\"frag3\" aria-label=\"Seeded cut illustration, no transaction\"><div class=\"mini\" id=\"mini\"><span class=\"mono\">Child key 0xfbd3\u202616c1</span><span class=\"badge live\" id=\"minibadge\">Active</span></div></div>\n        <div><h3>Cut access</h3><p>Revoke the keys you don't trust. The network refuses their next payment.</p></div>\n      </li>\n    </ol>\n  </section>\n\n  <section class=\"wrap faq\" id=\"questions\">\n    <div><h2>Questions</h2></div>\n    <div>\n      <details open><summary>Is Keycut read-only?</summary><p>Looking up an account only reads public chain data. No transaction is signed during a lookup.</p></details>\n      <details><summary>Do I need a wallet?</summary><p>Not to look. The owner command is available on every active key. Testnet account pages let the connected owner cut access after a confirmation and a getKey check. Mainnet account pages stay read-only until its wallet gate passes.</p></details>\n      <details><summary>Why doesn't revoking an admin key cut its child keys?</summary><p>Tempo's specification says revoking an admin key doesn't revoke the keys it authorised. Each key has to be revoked on its own.</p></details>\n      <details><summary>How complete is the list?</summary><p>Every lookup states the block range it covered. If any range couldn't be read, Keycut says so instead of showing a partial list as complete.</p></details>\n      <details><summary>Is the demo real money?</summary><p>No. The demo runs on Tempo testnet with test AlphaUSD, which has no value.</p></details>\n      <details><summary>What does High risk mean?</summary><p>An active key with no spending cap, no call restrictions, or no limit on who it can pay.</p></details>\n    </div>\n  </section>\n</main>"